      "Every job in the pipeline succeeded, so it is green. It still breaks the requirement: deploy ran on branch 'koans-08-branch-filters', not 'production'. That happened because the deploy entry in the build-test-and-deploy workflow has no branch filter. Its only condition is 'requires: [test-production]', which controls job order, not which branches can run it. Branch eligibility is set by adding 'filters: branches: only: production' to the deploy entry in the workflow's jobs list. Filters belong in the workflow job configuration, not the top-level job definition. An 'only' allowlist states the requirement exactly; an 'ignore' list would have to name every non-production branch. The build and test-production jobs can keep running on all branches."
