{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Beta tag filters needed on all jobs",
    "Explanation": [
      "The frozen run (pipeline #156) was API-triggered on the branch koans-09-tag-filters, and every job passed, so the pipeline is green. The behaviour does not meet the requirement, though.",
      "",
      "1. The config has no filters on any workflow job.",
      "2. CircleCI does not run workflow jobs for tag pushes unless a job has an explicit `filters.tags` entry. So a beta tag push would not run build, test or deploy.",
      "3. Without filters, deploy runs on every branch push, which is what happened in the frozen run. That breaks the rule that only beta tags should trigger deployment.",
      "4. A tag filter on deploy alone is not enough. CircleCI requires every upstream job in the `requires` chain (build and test) to have a matching tag filter too; otherwise the tagged workflow cannot reach deploy.",
      "",
      "The fix is therefore to add `filters: { tags: { only: /^beta.*/ } }` to all three jobs in the workflow. This lets build, test and deploy take part in beta-tagged runs and excludes non-beta tags. Adding `branches: { ignore: /.*/ }` as well would limit deployment to tags only. The exact beta pattern is assumed; the artifacts do not state it."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
